    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 14.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ healde man ælces Sunnandæges freolsunge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.24"/> fram Sæternesdæges none oð Monandæges lihtingce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.25"/> ⁊ ælcne oðerne mæssedæg, swa he beboden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.26"/> beo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>ælces Sunnandæges freolsunga fram Sæternesdæges none oð Monandæges lihtinge ⁊ ælcne oþerne <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#missing"/>mæssedæg, swa he bebodan beo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>. . . mæssedæge, swa he beboden beo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>in feriatione diei Dominicę ab hora nona Sabbati adusque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.16"/> diluculum secundę ferię et in sanctorum omnium sollempnitatibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.17"/>, sicut a sacerdote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.18"/> fuerint nuntiatę.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Dieique Dominice uacacio teneatur a nona Sabbati usque ad diluculum diei Lune, sic et omnis festi, sicut indictum est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="14.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="166" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ healde man<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_14-2.robnote.fn.2"/> ælces Sunnandæges freolsunge fram Sæternesdæges none oð Monandæges lihtingce ⁊ ælcne oðerne mæssedæg<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_14-2.robnote.fn.3"/> swa he beboden beo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="244" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And healde man ælces Sunnandæges freolsunge fram Sæternesdæges none oð Monandæges lihtingce, and ælcne oðerne mæssedæg, swa he beboden beo.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Und man halte die Feier jedes Sonntags vom Mittag des Sonnabends bis zum Morgenroth des Montags und jedes andere Kirchenfest, wie es geboten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_14-2.lnote.de.2"/> ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let the festival of every Sunday be kept from Saturday noon until Monday dawn, and every other mass-day, as it is commanded.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_14-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="167" ed="#robertson"/>And the festival of every Sunday shall be observed from noon on Saturday till dawn on Monday, and every other feast-day as has been prescribed<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_14-2.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="245" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And each Sunday holy day is to be observed from midafternoon on Saturday until dawn on Monday, and every other feast day just as is ordained for it.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="295"><ref target="clause:IIEg_5">II Eg 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Eg. 5</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_5">II Eg 5</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 14:2: (Cn 1020 18, HomN XXIII) (Hom N L) II Eg 5</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn1020_18">Cn 1020 18</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 14:2: (Cn 1020 18, HomN XXIII) (Hom N L) II Eg 5</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="347"><label>closer to</label> <ref target="clause:Cn1020_16">Cn 1020 16–18</ref> <quote>The phrasing of 16 – 18 also echoes HomN L ... and is closer to I Cn 14:2 – 16 than to anything earlier</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Here B (CCCC 383 f. 43, c. 1125) begins in the old hand; the quire with I Cn 1–14.2 is torn out (pp. 42c–o hold a 16th-c. copy from A). Liebermann compares II Eg 5.; Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 295, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">And healde man: omitted A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">mæssedæg: start of B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ga <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ga Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. ad <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. ad Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tate <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tate K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tibus <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tibus K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Folgendes bis 15 benutzen, der AB-Klasse näher, <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 117. 208</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">What follows, up to 15, is used by <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 117. 208, closer to the AB class</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_14-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dass Pfarrer Feste ankündigt, bemerkt Q auch zu II Eg 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">That the parish priest announces feasts is noted by Q also at II Eg 5</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_14-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II Edg. 5 etc.; Wulfstan, pp. 117, 208.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_14-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sicut a sacerdote nuntiatae</hi>, Q, cf. II Edg. 5, Q.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_14-2.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><label>rihtlice</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">r.—man</hi> om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_14-2.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><label>mæssedæg</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">At this point (with the word <hi rend="italic">mæssedæg</hi>) B begins and is used here for the remainder of I Cn.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
